%N A401484 Numbers whose largest square unitary divisor is a fourth power.
%C A401484 Subsequence of A337050 and first differs from it at n = 49: A337050(49) = 64 is not a term in this sequence.
%C A401484 Differs from A304364 by having the terms 1, 216, 432, 648, 864, 1000, ..., and not having the terms 64, 192, 320, 448, 704, 729, 832, 960, ... .
%C A401484 Numbers k such that A350388(k) is a fourth power.
%C A401484 Numbers whose prime factorization exponents are not congruent to 2 (mod 4) (i.e., they are terms in A042965).
%C A401484 The asymptotic density of this sequence is Product_{p prime} ((1 + p^2 + p^3)/(1 + p + p^2 + p^3)) = zeta(4) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^2 + 1/p^3 - 1/p^4) = 0.74061963657217328604... .
%H A401484 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A401484/b401484.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%t A401484 q[k_] := AllTrue[FactorInteger[k][[;; , 2]], Mod[#, 4] != 2 &]; Select[Range[90], q]
%o A401484 (PARI) isok(k) = #select(e -> (e%4 == 2), factor(k)[, 2]) == 0;
%Y A401484 Subsequence of A337050.
%Y A401484 A401485 is a subsequence.
